      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "After a 2 month delay and finding it very difficult and frustrating in getting installation updates I’m happy with the final result.During the sign on process the salesman was happy to call me two or three times a day even on weekends. Once I signed in he was in contactable.Found it very difficult to extract a start date from them.Finally got hold of the boss, Nick and he gave me a firm date.Tbh just a simple bit of feedback during the process would have allayed my concerns and I would have been happy enough to accept any delays.Once Nick called I was ok with his update and he even gave me a further discount as a sweetener.The hardware installed matched the quote, including the free installation of a smart relay.The installation itself was pretty good and very quickly installed, half a day!  Although my house doesn’t have a crying space and rather than lift sheets to run conduit through to the board they’ve run it on the roof surface. Not a big fan of that.The system is a 13.2 kw using Trina solar vertex panels and a 3 phase 10kw Sungrow inverter.All working good and producing plenty of juice.My only advice to Countryside would be to lift your customer feedback, everything else runs pretty well.",
